personality test,

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.801
why do you go with
Meyers-Jackal?

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.400
Little on the nose.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.334
All right,
we've talked a lot about

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:33.400
why you're watching YouTube
if you don't like this.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.834
Like why you're watching this
on YouTube,

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.934
if you don't like this with
so many options on YouTube

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.100
and this is a couple
of weeks ago now,

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.767
I said when you walk
into a grocery store,

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.200
do you just take the first thing
that you see?

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.534
And I'm like, "Oh, tuna fish."

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.667
And then you said, "You
obviously don't grocery shop

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.334
because tuna fish
is never the first thing

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:47.367
you see in the grocery store."

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.501
And then last week I said,

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.000
"Well, actually,
it's the first thing I see

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.667
because I use a VIP entrance
and it opens up into seafood."

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:53.901
And then a lot of you said,

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.868
"This also proves
you don't go to a grocery store

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.667
because tuna fish is not
in the seafood section,

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:00.400
it's in the canned
goods section."

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.634
And to that,
all I want to say is,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.234
you got me.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.968
I don't go to
the grocery store.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:13.767
You know where I get my tuna?

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:16.634
The Omakase menu
at Takasawi's.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:26.267
I said "IE" last week
and was told,

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.367
one does not say "IE" out loud.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:31.434
You use IE in writing
and when speaking,

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.567
you say that is.

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:36.133
Which means the correct way
to sing "Old MacDonald" is

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.634
Old MacDonald
had a farm, E that is IO.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.167
I had a little bit of fun
last week.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.100
I had a bit of fun last week
obliquely referencing

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.100
the lyrics
to the Barenaked Ladies song

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.834
"If I Had $1,000,000"
and I reference

00:03:55.834 --> 00:04:00.100
Barenaked Ladies lyrics
the reason anyone would --

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.400
click bait.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.400
I referenced the line,

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.667
"I'd buy you
John Merrick's remains."

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:08.334
And it's been one week
since I did that,

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:10.601
and many of you

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:13.767
looked at me

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.234
cocked your head to the side
and said, I'm angry.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.968
Is it because when you
were angry,

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.934
because while in the film,

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.234
The Elephant Man
is named John Merrick,

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:27.267
in real life,
his name was Joseph Merrick.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.601
And -- but I was --
I was quoting the lyric,

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:32.300
it should be noted correctly.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.801
But Joseph Merrick
was his real name.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:40.000
And I guess France --
Frederick, excuse me,

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.968
Frederick Treves,
the surgeon who wrote the book,

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:44.067
is the one -- he actually --
he got it wrong.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.100
I guess he got it wrong
maybe just by accident.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.300
He maybe wasn't that good
on the details

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.167
when writing this story

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.334
about Joseph Merrick because
someone wrote -- someone said,

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:55.834
it's actually Joseph Merrick,

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:59.968
and he changed it to John
to protect his identity.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:03.634
Feel like that's not enough
of a change.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:07.100
It's like I'm writing a book
about you, but don't worry.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.734
I'm changing your name to John.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:15.200
So we're going to call
Frederick Treves,

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.934
Francis from now on.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:20.601
Good back up.

