Who would it benefit?
It's not like there's ads.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.300
I mean, I'm --
I'm reading it right.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.968
If the correction segment...

00:09:14.968 --> 00:09:17.367
Two or three minutes.
Don't pad it out. Yeah.

00:09:21.434 --> 00:09:24.267
The nerve.

00:09:24.267 --> 00:09:26.000
Because this -- I mean, again,
it's not for the show, but...

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.501
There's an integrity to this.

00:09:35.267 --> 00:09:37.501
Pad it out.

00:09:43.767 --> 00:09:47.634
I mentioned my new book

00:09:47.634 --> 00:09:49.033
"I'm Not Scared, YOU'RE scared!"

00:09:49.033 --> 00:09:51.701
It's a very proud --
I'm very proud of it.

00:09:51.701 --> 00:09:53.200
And one of the things
I'm proudest about,

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.834
and I've mentioned
this on the show

00:09:55.834 --> 00:09:57.300
is the groundbreaking choice
I made.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.934
It's the first children's book

00:09:59.934 --> 00:10:04.200
to have both a rabbit
and a bear in it.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.334
And a lot of you
have written me

00:10:05.334 --> 00:10:07.801
that's not true.

00:10:07.801 --> 00:10:11.200
And you wouldn't give me
examples of books that

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.100
have both a bear and a rabbit.

00:10:15.801 --> 00:10:17.400
But here's something
that is true.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:21.367
The time it took you to write
that you'll never get back.

00:10:30.434 --> 00:10:32.434
Oh, this is great.
I mean, this is what --

00:10:32.434 --> 00:10:33.667
this is my...
[ speaks indistinctly ]

00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:34.868
I got a correction
from way back.

00:10:34.868 --> 00:10:37.133
2021 corrections.

00:10:37.133 --> 00:10:38.901
We talked about -- someone
clarified the difference

00:10:38.901 --> 00:10:42.100
because we mixed up
Alice Cooper's chicken

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.167
and Ozzy Osbourne's bat,

00:10:44.167 --> 00:10:47.334
and someone really put the time
into a long correction

00:10:47.334 --> 00:10:49.934
